          "message": "test(velvet): fold literal-only duplicate cases into rows and share the allocation canary (#1351)\n\n## What & why\n\nThis change shrinks repeated test source without changing which cases run.\n\n**Literal-only duplicates folded into rows.** Eleven groups of methods were identical once literals are normalised: same comments, same attributes, and no `Assume`. Each group is now one parameterised method with one `[TestCase]` row per former method.\n- `VirtualListSizingAndScrollTests`: 5 groups, 15 methods become 5.\n- `ArbitraryValueTests`: 5 groups, 23 methods become 5.\n- `GapParityTests`: 1 group, 2 methods become 1.\n\nEach row keeps its former method name as `TestName`. The executed case names are therefore unchanged, and so is everything keyed on them: `neuter_holes.txt`, `assume_gate_baseline.txt` and the mutation ledgers. Counted from the `[Test]` and `[TestCase]` attributes, the package has 9144 cases before and after, with 29 fewer methods.\n\n**The copied canary is shared.** The known-array allocation canary was copied byte-for-byte into eight fixtures. Its body now lives once in `TestUtilities/GCAllocationCanary.BlocksForKnownArray()`. Each of the eight fixtures still runs and asserts its own canary case, so a run filtered to one fixture still proves the probe counts. It is a separate class because `GCAllocationProbeSurfaceTests` pins the probe's own public surface.\n\nThe changed cases carry `GREEN_ON_BASE(refactor)` declarations, since the fold preserves what each case asserts.\n\nRefs #1347\n\n## Remaining\n\n- Groups whose comments differ were left alone. Folding them would drop the rationale each case carries. `GapParityTests` and `ArbitraryValueTests` still hold such groups.\n- Identical-comment groups in other fixtures are left for a follow-up, for example `GradientStopListTests`, `AncestorDescendantStoreRerenderTests` and `GradientBoxAspectTests`.\n- Groups with `Assume` gates were left alone, as were the canaries of a different shape (`CaptureEventBindingTests`, `ElementFactoryEventsAllocTests`).\n- The redundancy report from #1347, which works out removal candidates from mutation and coverage subsumption, is not part of this change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable):\n  - generator suite;\n  - duplication, assume-gate and stranded-name checks;\n  - `--refusals`;\n  - `neuter_check --validate` / `--audit`;\n  - `base_red_check --plan` and its own test suite.\n  - The Unity suites run in CI.\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it. No new tests were added: every changed case is a behaviour-preserving fold, declared `refactor`.\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches. There is no doc impact; no markdown names a removed method.\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment: none, since this is test-only.\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria. They stay on #1347.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
