          "id": "76750e26870d0e0580c668d9571949fae5f8966a",
          "message": "fix(velvet): revert UseOptimistic entries in the commit that lands the transition (#1367)\n\n## What & why\n\nWhen a transition settled, `Hooks.UseOptimistic` reverted a holder's entries only through a Normal-lane render requested by `HookSlots.RetireEntriesOwnedBy`. That render ran in a later drain wave, after the settling commit's layout effects. Two cases were affected:\n- a holder that the landing drain does not render;\n- a holder rendered ahead of a descendant whose subsumption settles the transition.\n\nIn both, a layout effect of the settling commit read the holder, and the components reading its value, with the entries still in place.\n\nReact 19.1 does not do this. `dispatchOptimisticSetState` gives the optimistic update `revertLane: requestTransitionLane(transition)`. `updateReducerImpl` then skips it in that lane's render, so every holder drops the entries in the transition's own commit.\n\n**The change:**\n- `FiberWorkLoop.FlushState` and `ContinueReconcile` open an owed-render window through a shared helper.\n- `RetireEntriesOwnedBy` records each holder in it (`OweSettleRender`).\n- Right after `SettleCompletedTransition`, and before the commit's layout effects, each recorded holder that holds an immediate-tier lane is flushed. This covers three places:\n  - a drain's flush;\n  - the terminal slice of a time-sliced reconcile;\n  - the time-sliced abort path, before `OnRenderError`.\n- A holder that is unmounted, hidden under a fallback or in a detached host keeps its render for the scheduler. So does a settle that no flush lands, such as an `async` action completing.\n\n**Docs and changelog.** The `useOptimistic` row of `react-migration.md` and the `UseOptimistic` XML doc state the new behaviour, and the deviation sentence is gone. A changelog fragment is under `unreleased/`.\n\n**Tests.** `UseOptimisticRevertCommitTests` adds five cases. Each one reads the holder and its reader from a layout effect or fallback of the settling commit, and folds the pre-settle reading into the asserted tuple. All five are expected red on main:\n- a holder the landing drain does not render;\n- a holder rendered ahead of a subsumed descendant that settles the transition;\n- a flush outside every drain;\n- a time-sliced terminal slice;\n- a resumed slice throwing past every in-pass boundary.\n\nCloses #1318\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
